4. Source File Styles
You can use export/import in all your GAS logic files.
You do not need to manually attach classes/functions to globalThis.CAMPAIGN in source files.
Webpack will handle the global assignment in the output bundle.
<hr></hr>
5. Best Practice Moving Forward
Author all code using TypeScript modules (export/import).
Use "module": "ESNext" in your TypeScript config for GAS.
Rely on Webpack to bundle and attach everything to globalThis.CAMPAIGN.
Remove manual global assignments from source files over time.
<hr></hr>
6. Client-Side Includes
For client-side includes (<?!= include(...) ?>), use the same approach:
Author with modules.
Use Webpack to bundle and attach to the global object.
